A||N||4||hugh|| Need V8 exhaust help||||1||
Z||000000||hugh||03-09-2001||06:48 AM||||As some of you know,I have a longitudinal mounted V8 in my 88GT.I'm doing the suspension and  adding AFR heads with a Lingenfelter Superam fuel injection settup to the engine.I need shorty headers that go more back than down so I can put them on facing the front and make a 180 degree turn on the exhaust to go out the back.The S10 headers(from Hedman) look like they may work,but I can't be sure.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula 18||03-09-2001||10:38 AM||||Check out rockcrawl's website. He's got a page about a long v8. I think there is a page about how to make a set of headers from a weld up kit. The look Schweeeet!! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||03-09-2001||04:14 PM||||I used a Heddman weld-up kit. It comes with the flanges, collectors, and enough bent pipe for just about any configuration. Cost was around $150 from Summit. It requires a little more work but you can make them exactly the way you want them.<P>The S-10 headers I've seen are two piece on the drivers side for steering shaft clearance. How 'bout shorty headers for a late model Camaro?<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||Raydar||03-09-2001||04:55 PM||||I was wondering about the Camaro headers, too. Don't really know that much about 'em though. <BR>Check Sanderson's site. They can build whatever you want. <A HREF="http://www.sandersonheaders.com/custombuiltheaders.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sandersonheaders.com/custombuiltheaders.htm</A> <BR> <BR>Okay... did some more looking. <A HREF="http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/cs11.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/cs11.htm</A>  <BR>This is the S-10 Sanderson. It is also available in 1 5/8" size.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||03-10-2001||05:49 PM||||Thanks for the responses,very much appreciated!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
